message:
Now I can see the vulnerability. Let me analyze `lex_multiline_string`:

```c
static void *lex_multiline_string(struct lexer *lexer)
{
    char *end = (peek(lexer) == '"') ? "\"\"\"" : "'''";

    advance_n(lexer, strlen("'''") - 1);

    do {
        if (!strncmp(lexer->pos, end, 3)) {
            emit(lexer, LEXEME_STRING);
            lexer->pos += 3;

            return lex_config;
        }
    } while (next(lexer) != '\0');

    return lex_error(lexer, "EOF while scanning multiline string");
}
```

The issue: `strncmp(lexer->pos, end, 3)` reads 3 bytes from `lexer->pos` without checking if there are at least 3 bytes remaining in the buffer. If the input ends with `'''` or `"""` at the very end of the buffer (or near the end), `strncmp` will read past the end of the buffer, causing a global-buffer-overflow READ.

Let me look at the lexer structure and how the buffer is set up.

<｜｜DSML｜｜>
<parameter=command>sed -n '1,250p' /workspace/repo-vul/src-vul/lwan/src/lib/lwan-config.c</parameter>
</｜｜DSML｜｜>

